% The quickstart IOU: issue, transfer, split, merge, and a delivery-versus-payment trade
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% from its source: each template a fluent keyed by the contract id, each create and choice an action,
% who may do what integrity constraints. The source is kept in sources/ (File > Show the Original in the
% Logical English editor, View > The original this was converted from in the LPS2 IDE).
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the legal view
% (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program in the Logical English editor, View > Legal view in the LPS2 IDE).
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 27.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the iou *an iou* with issuer *an issuer*, owner *an owner*, currency *a currency*, amount *an amount* and observers party list *an observers party list*; known as create_iou.
    *a party* creates the iou transfer *an iou transfer* with iou issuer *an iou issuer*, iou owner *an iou owner*, iou currency *an iou currency*, iou amount *an iou amount*, iou observers party list *an iou observers party list* and new owner *a new owner*; known as create_iou_transfer.
    *a party* creates the iou trade *an iou trade* with buyer *a buyer*, seller *a seller*, base iou cid *a base iou cid*, base issuer *a base issuer*, base currency *a base currency*, base amount *a base amount*, quote issuer *a quote issuer*, quote currency *a quote currency* and quote amount *a quote amount*; known as create_iou_trade.
    *a party* archives the iou *an iou*; known as archive_iou.
    *a party* archives the iou transfer *an iou transfer*; known as archive_iou_transfer.
    *a party* archives the iou trade *an iou trade*; known as archive_iou_trade.
    *a party* exercises split on the iou *an iou* with split amount *a split amount* creating *a second iou* and *a third iou*; known as iou_split.
    *a party* exercises merge on the iou *an iou* with other cid *an other cid* creating *a second iou*; known as iou_merge.
    *a party* exercises transfer on the iou *an iou* with new owner *a new owner* creating *an iou transfer*; known as iou_transfer.
    *a party* exercises cancel on the iou transfer *an iou transfer* creating *an iou*; known as iou_transfer_cancel.
    *a party* exercises reject on the iou transfer *an iou transfer* creating *an iou*; known as iou_transfer_reject.
    *a party* exercises accept on the iou transfer *an iou transfer* creating *an iou*; known as iou_transfer_accept.
    *a party* exercises accept on the iou trade *an iou trade* with quote iou cid *a quote iou cid* creating *an iou* and *a second iou*; known as iou_trade_accept.
    *a party* exercises trade proposal reject on the iou trade *an iou trade*; known as trade_proposal_reject.

the fluents are:
    *an iou* is an iou with issuer *an issuer*, owner *an owner*, currency *a currency*, amount *an amount* and observers party list *an observers party list*; known as iou.
    *an iou transfer* is an iou transfer with iou issuer *an iou issuer*, iou owner *an iou owner*, iou currency *an iou currency*, iou amount *an iou amount*, iou observers party list *an iou observers party list* and new owner *a new owner*; known as iou_transfer.
    *an iou trade* is an iou trade with buyer *a buyer*, seller *a seller*, base iou cid *a base iou cid*, base issuer *a base issuer*, base currency *a base currency*, base amount *a base amount*, quote issuer *a quote issuer*, quote currency *a quote currency* and quote amount *a quote amount*; known as iou_trade.

the knowledge base quickstart includes:

the text of "the source daml/Iou.daml" is at "sources/daml/Iou.daml".

the text of "the source daml/IouTrade.daml" is at "sources/daml/IouTrade.daml".

the text of "the source daml/Tests/Iou.daml" is at "sources/daml/Tests/Iou.daml".

the text of "the source daml/Tests/Trade.daml" is at "sources/daml/Tests/Trade.daml".

% Iou: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the iou an iou with issuer an issuer, owner an owner, currency a currency, amount an amount and observers party list an observers party list
then the iou is an iou with issuer the issuer, owner the owner, currency the currency, amount the amount and observers party list the observers party list.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the iou an iou with issuer an issuer, owner an owner, currency a currency, amount an amount and observers party list an observers party list
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the iou an iou with issuer an issuer, owner an owner, currency a currency, amount an amount and observers party list an observers party list
    and the party is different from the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the iou an iou with issuer an issuer, owner an owner, currency a currency, amount an amount and observers party list an observers party list
    and the amount <= 0.0.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the iou an iou with issuer an issuer, owner an owner, currency a currency, amount an amount and observers party list an observers party list
    and the iou is an iou with issuer a second issuer, owner a second owner, currency a second currency, amount a second amount and observers party list a second observers party list.

